Entry 2: Bottom Navigation Bar & Navigator Routing Issue

Date: October 28, 2026
Tool: Gemini
Prompt/Query: "How do I switch tabs in a Flutter BottomNavigationBar without pushing duplicate screens onto the Navigator stack? I current have it set on each page vs having a menu file to be inherited on each page, but when i test, the clicks don't work and take me to another page"
Output & Application: Basically told me to replace Navigator.push() calls inside the onTap handler with an _currentIndex state variable that updates the body using IndexedStack (or a switch statement). 
Update: Still not working so I tried a new chat and I know I am mapping _currentIndex = index; correctly, inside your onTap handler, the body is hardcoded to your home page SafeArea / SingleChildScrollView. 
This is basically why the buttons will animate but not change the screen and navigate away. 
Output: "How to Fix It: To make your bottom navigation actually switch between your Home, History, and Settings screens, your body needs to respond to _currentIndex. You need to isolate your home body: 
Take all the widgets inside your current body: SafeArea(child: SingleChildScrollView(...)) and move them into a separate helper method (like Widget _buildHomeContent()). This keeps your main build method clean.
You need to list your tabs: Right above your return Scaffold(), you need to set up a list of your screens (final List<Widget> pages = [_buildHomeContent(...), const HistoryScreen(), const SettingsScreen()];) 
so your app knows what options it has. You need to swap out the scaffold body: Inside your return Scaffold(...), you need to change your static body: property so it points to an IndexedStack instead, 
passing it your _currentIndex variable (body: IndexedStack(index: _currentIndex, children: pages)).You need to keep your navigation bar intact: You don't need to change your bottomNavigationBar at all
because your onTap handler is already successfully updating _currentIndex whenever a user clicks an icon!If you used a normal conditional check or list lookup, switching tabs would destroy the old 
page and recreate it from scratch.
Learning: I was thinking of buttons and refering to the hallowween assignment and may have been confused with the navigation as i tried to fix myself. A Scaffold body that is hardcoded to a single static
view won't change when I tap the low menu. The body had no dynamic list or `IndexedStack` to render different screens even though they were made and main had a tiny job. 


